  most trustworthy celestial spirits are  aquarius and leo  in a fight leo is the safer choice as  the water bearer is typically a  temperamental mess  who despite being powerful fights in a  way that causes a lot of trouble to lucy  often out of her own volition however  facing insurmountable odds in the battle  against tartaros  lucy's forced to make the ultimate  sacrifice in order to summon the  celestial spirit king  break aquarius's key despite reaffirming  her disdain for lucy the water bearer  still cries along with her master  taking in the fact that she would never  see lucy again while she retains her  temperamental attitude towards the  celestial spirit mage  aquarius at this final moment reconciles  with her master  only to be shut off from the mortal  realm for good  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  [Applause]  for our seventh moment we have vegeta  blowing himself up in an attempt to take  down majin buu at the time of his  introduction  vegeta was shown to be ruthless and  uncaring he didn't give a damn about  anything but strength  all in all you can see why his eventual  decision to sacrifice himself in the buu  saga is one of the most gripping moments  of that arc  despite not caring about bulma and  trunks it's obvious that the prince of  saiyans is lying and that he's already  completed the character development that  prompts him  to sacrifice himself for the world  vegeta realizes the consequences of all  his previous  actions and decides to blow himself up  going down in a literal blaze of glory  he makes the choice of dying for the  world in an act of personal redemption  [Applause]  me  [Music]  oh  at number six it's rider's doom battle  against gilgamesh from  fate zero if there's a list of all-time  fake anime moments  rider's battle against gilgamesh would  surely make him  this fight has it all glorious noble  phantasms  heartwarming farewell speeches and  gilgamesh finally finding a worthy  opponent  most of all it showcases the fire of  determination burning with invite  assault in one climactic battle  even while finding himself completely  outmatched against the king of heroes  ryder charges on taking everything that  the gate of babylon can toss at him  his sheer will pushes him on but he was  finally put down for good  at the fifth spot we have a sacrificing  his life for luffy  being a storyline revolving around  saving luffy's brother part of the  climax of the marine foot arc ends with  a cloud of despair looming over our  heroes  akainu gets the upper hand on ace and  moves to finish off luffy  it's then the ace steps in and takes the  blow for his brother  one that would ultimately kill him  instead of possibly living on full of  regret ace makes the decision to die in  an act of protecting luffy  he doesn't die in a lost battle against  someone out of his own league but on his  own terms  it could feel unfair especially to one  piece fans but ace's death has a legacy  in it that it finally convinces luffy  that he has to keep getting stronger  [Music]  foreign  irwin smith's sacrifice against the  beast titan ranks fourth on the list  while the commander of the survey corps  did care for his men  he's ruthless and wouldn't hesitate in  sacrificing them for the betterment of  mankind  needless to say the commander is someone  who's caused the deaths of hundreds of  people  soon though he reflects on his actions  and realizes that he's been a hypocrite  all along he's unwilling to die for the  greater cause  while preaching that ideology to justify  his orders and the inner desire that's  fueled by a moment with his father  it's this realization that drives him to  lead the charge against the beast titan  this distraction gives levi the opening  needed to confront and defeat zeke  and in the end it's irwin's desire to  die with the fallen recruits that pushes  levi to save the lethally wounded armin  instead  leaving him to die after a moment of  redemption  [Music]  three we have jiraya giving up his life  in the battle against  payne during his infiltration mission  jiraiya finds himself in the battle  against konam  it turns out that he has his work cut  out not only does he have to contend  with conan he has to fight for his life  against pain  or what's supposed to be pain it's then  that he finds out that pain is actually  an  entity composed of multiple bodies armed  with unique powers  despite his valiant efforts uriah finds  himself overwhelmed by the pains  there's hope at the end of the master  ninja's life he dies not with sadness or  regrets but with a smile  knowing that he's done his part in his  last moments he entrusts the world to  the pupil who he knows would soon carve  his spot in history  as the savior of the world  [Music]  sacrifice at the end of code geass takes  the second spot on the list  still held as one of the most iconic  endings to a legendary series  it would be hard to top lelouch's  sacrifice at the end of code gyas  taking in the hatred of the world and  directing it towards him as an  all-powerful demagogue lelouch finishes  his long-time plan with suzaku by having  suzaku take the guise of zero  and kill him truly a gutsy plan at the  cost  of the greatest sacrifice given  everything else has happened would  anything less have sufficed with the one  focus of hatred gone  lelouch cements himself as a messianic  archetype one who has paid the ultimate  price to save the world  [Music]  oh  me  the number one sacrifice in anime  belongs to isaac naterro  one of the most defining and my personal  favorite battle in chimera ant arc  is the one between chimera and king  meruem and isaac nataro  chairman of the hunter association it's  a battle of two  very powerful characters at peak  performance despite his withered state  and vulnerability after being  overpowered  natero manages to strike fear in  meruem's heart claiming the latter knows  nothing about humanity's endless  potential for evolution and malice  nutero then